!! <<id [[TiddlyTools/Time/Timers]]>> <<top>>
<<<
''Displays a list of task timers to record starting, ending, elapsed and total accumulated times.''
<br>Optional: [[TiddlyTools/Time/Ticker]], [[TiddlyTools/Time/action-timeout.js]], [[TiddlyTools/Time/Setup]], <$link to=<<tt_time_config>>/>
<br>Examples: [[SampleTimers]]

* To add a timer to the list, enter a timername and optional description, and press <<button {{$:/core/images/new-button}}>>.
* If no timername is entered, a default name will be used (Timer, Timer 1, Timer 2, etc.)
* <<button {{$:/core/images/timestamp-on}}>> starts a timer "session".  The elapsed time is displayed and automatically updated in real-time.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/timestamp-off}}>> stops the current timer session.  The total accumulated time is displayed.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/cancel-button}}>> cancels the current timer session.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/refresh-button}}>> clears saved timer sessions.  You will be asked to confirm before the data is cleared.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/chevron-down}}>> shows/hides a table with the starting, ending, elapsed and total time for each timer session.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/delete-button}}>> deletes the timer and all associated session data.  You will be asked to confirm before the tiddler is deleted.
* <<button {{$:/core/images/edit-button}}>> adds or edits a short text comment associated with a specific timer session.
* You can also click directly on any existing comment text to begin editing that comment.
* While editing a comment, <<button {{$:/core/images/delete-button}}>> deletes the comment, <<button {{$:/core/images/close-button}}>> or <kbd>escape</kbd> discards changes to the comment, <<button {{$:/core/images/done-button}}>> or <kbd>enter</kbd> saves the comment.
* Each timer is stored in an individual tiddler with a default prefix of `$:/config/Timers/` followed by the timername.
* To show the timer interface in another tiddler, use `<<timers>>`.
* To create a separate set of timers with a different prefix (e.g., "~MyTimers"), use `<$vars timer_config="MyTimers"><<timers>></$vars>`.
* You can set the format used to display the starting and stopping time (see [[TiddlyTools/Time/Setup]] or <$link to=<<tt_time_config>>/>).
* //Note:// if the [[Ticker|TiddlyTools/Time/Ticker]] or [[action-timeout.js|TiddlyTools/Time/action-timeout.js]] are not installed, the elapsed time will not be updated in real-time, but will still be recorded correctly when <<button {{$:/core/images/timestamp-off}}>> is pressed.
* You can also use the following macros to create custom output showing only specific interface elements:<div>

|`<<timer_add>>`|Shows timername and description inputs with <<button {{$:/core/images/new-button}}>> button.|
|`<<timer_list>>`|Shows the list of all currently defined timers.|
|`<<timer timername>>`|Shows a single timer for a specific task.|
|`<<timer_buttons timername>>`|Shows start, stop and reset buttons.|
|`<<timer_elapsed timername>>`|Shows the elapsed time for the current timer session.|
|`<<timer_total timername>>`|Shows the total accumulated time for all timer sessions.|
|`<<timer_history timername>>`|Shows a table with the starting, ending, elapsed, and total time for each timer session.|
* If you omit the `timername` parameter, the timer information is stored in the current tiddler.
* If you specify the `timername` parameter, the timer information is stored in a separate tiddler with that timername.
</div>
